WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.120
So a custom GPT is made up of a name,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.200
instructions that tell the GPT what to do,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.760
sometimes files for the GPT to reference,

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.960
sometimes apps, although that's not a
requirement,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.200
and then some custom GPTs have

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.480
been configured with custom actions.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.840
I want to highlight that custom actions do
not

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.680
transfer over when you migrate to a
plugin.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.160
When I hit that "Migrate" button,

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.120
you'll see that the name of the custom GPT

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.680
becomes the name of the skill within the
plugin.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.380
The instructions and files are within that
skill.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.880
If you've connected an app,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.640
it just connects right to the plugin,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.080
and then those custom actions again are
not transferred.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.480
So you'll either need to set up

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.440
a supported app with the right read or
write actions,

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.800
or you'll need to set up a custom MCP
server.
